    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Amid a significant reduction in headcount, the 3,000 displaced workers are left to bear the cost of 'reinvention.' This organizational downsizing, a bloodletting of nearly one-fifth of the workforce, was framed as a necessary business strategy. The corporate entity's decree handed down from the top leaves communities like Reno and Woodland Hills facing site closures, their abandoned workspaces a testament to corporate flight.",
